									<td class="content-block" style="font-family: 'Helvetica Neue', Helvetica, Arial, sans-serif; box-sizing: border-box; font-size: 14px; vertical-align: top; margin: 0; padding: 0 0 20px;" valign="top">
										Hi {!Lead.FirstName},
									</td>
								</tr>
								<tr style="font-family: 'Helvetica Neue', Helvetica, Arial, sans-serif; box-sizing: border-box; font-size: 14px; margin: 0;">
									<td class="content-block" style="font-family: 'Helvetica Neue', Helvetica, Arial, sans-serif; box-sizing: border-box; font-size: 14px; vertical-align: top; margin: 0; padding: 0 0 20px;" valign="top">
										Join EverQuote and RPOA (Role Play at the Olson Agency) from 2:00 to 3:00 PM ET (11:00 AM PT), Wednesday, February 5, 2020 for a LIVE role-play webinar on how to handle the objection “No thanks, you’re the 5th agent to call me....”  with agent Jeremy Olson, who currently runs 6 offices with over $30 million in premium written. Join Jeremy and insurance sales coach Kristin Isaacson for a live role-play session. They will share the best responses to use when faced with one of the most common objections heard with insurance leads – <b>“No thanks, you’re the 5th agent to call me...”
</b>
<br>
									<br>
										If you’ve ever called a lead only to be told “No thanks, you’re the 5th agent to call me....” you probably understand how this objection can shut down a conversation before it even starts. Having prepared responses will help you and your team increase your odds for success. Jeremy and Kristin will walk you through ways to overcome this objection by role-playing common scenarios live.
									</td>
								</tr>
                                <tr>
									<td>
										The webinar is free to join and will be hosted by <a href="https://www.insuranceroleplay.com">RPOA</a> and <a href="https://go.everquote.com/pro">EverQuote!</a>
<br>
<br>
You can sign-up for the free webinar here directly <a href=https://zoom.us/webinar/register/WN_FkoyaICeSY6PZVlNvYf2ew>through our link here!</a>
